%N A369626 a(n) is the number of permutations of [n] which avoid the patterns 1234, 1324, and 2413.
%H A369626 Carlo Corti, <a href="/A369626/b369626.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 0..400</a>
%H A369626 D. Callan, T. Mansour and M. Shattuck, <a href="https://doi.org/10.23638/DMTCS-19-1-5">Wilf classification of triples of 4-letter patterns I</a>, Discrete Math. Theor. Comput. Sci. 19:1 (2017), Paper No. 5, 35 pp.; <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/1605.04969">full version</a>, arXiv:1605.04969 [math.CO], 2016.
%H A369626 Carlo Corti, <a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21493903">A Formula-Derived Extension of OEIS A369626 Through n = 400</a>, Zenodo, 2026.
%H A369626 PermPAL, <a href="https://permpal.com/perms/basis/0123_0213_1302">Av(1234,1324,2413)</a>.
%H A369626 <a href="/index/Rec#order_04">Index entries for linear recurrences with constant coefficients</a>, signature (7,-16,14,-4).
%F A369626 From _Carlo Corti_, Jul 22 2026: (Start)
%F A369626 G.f.: (1 - 3*x + x^2)^2/((1 - x)*(1 - 2*x)*(1 - 4*x + 2*x^2)).
%F A369626 a(n) = 7*a(n-1) - 16*a(n-2) + 14*a(n-3) - 4*a(n-4) for n >= 5. (End)
%e A369626 All 6 of the permutations of length 3 avoid all patterns of length 4, so a(3)=6.
%t A369626 LinearRecurrence[{7, -16, 14, -4}, {1, 1, 2, 6, 21}, 30] (* _Paolo Xausa_, Jul 29 2026 *)
